sub:assertion {
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/genotype-correction-annotated-flying-fish-genome-exists> a delphi:Claim ;
    rdfs:label "Correction to this project's own published claim: an annotated flying-fish genome does exist, with 23,611 predicted protein-coding genes of which 23,492 (99.5%) carry a database hit, so what flying fish lack is not genes but expression and phenotype data" ;
    dct:description "Status: correction of a claim this project published; the corrected statement is supported by the cited paper, and the superseded statement was wrong. WHAT WE SAID. Until 2026-10-31 this thread's files and its public dashboard stated that \"almost no molecular data exists for flying fish\" and described the available genomic resource as merely \"one scaffold-level assembly (GCA_018398805.1)\". That wording was carried into the map's constraint line, the thread's README, the brief that ten subagents worked under, and the live status headline. WHAT THE SOURCE SAYS. Xu et al. 2021 (Frontiers in Genetics 12:695700, doi 10.3389/fgene.2021.695700) assembled the mirrorwing flyingfish Hirundichthys speculiger at 1.04 Gb in 3,052 scaffolds (contig N50 992.83 kb, scaffold N50 1152.47 kb; BUSCO 94.2% genome and 95.7% gene set on actinopterygii_odb9) and predicted 23,611 protein-coding genes, of which 23,492 (99.5%) carry at least one hit across KEGG (20,692), SwissProt (21,453), TrEMBL (23,477) and InterPro (21,888). That assembly is the very one this project was already citing as GCA_018398805.1: we had the right genome and described it too weakly. The annotation is downloadable (figshare doi 10.6084/m9.figshare.14600634.v1). WHAT CHANGED. The constraint now says that an annotated genome exists and that the gap is expression and phenotype, not genes. The proxy-species rule is unchanged but its justification is corrected: zebrafish and medaka are used because ZFIN-style expression and mutant-phenotype records exist only for them, not because flying-fish genes are unknown. WHAT IS STILL ABSENT, established by counting rather than by inference: the strings \"RNA-seq\" and \"transcriptome\" appear ZERO times in that paper's full text. It reports no expression data, no mutant, no kinetics and no regulatory network. AND A CAVEAT ON THE HEADLINE FIGURE: \"functionally annotated\" there means at least one sequence-similarity or domain hit and nothing more. TrEMBL alone supplies 23,477 of the hits and TrEMBL is automatically generated and unreviewed, so 99.5% measures database coverage, not understood function. This correction was caught by the project lead, not by the thread that published the error. What it does not establish: It does not establish that the flying fish is now a usable model: a gene list cannot say where a gene is expressed, what happens when it is lost, or at which stage it acts, which is what this project's map is built from. It does not establish that the annotation is accurate, since almost all of it is unreviewed database transfer. It does not establish that any particular gene of interest is present in that gene set: no orthologue call was made here, and that question is owned by another thread. And it says nothing about the species whose fins were measured. Pre-registration: none: a correction. The error was found by the project lead reading a primary source the thread had not read, and the thread then verified it rather than accepting the relay." ;
    delphi:context "The error mattered because it was load-bearing: it was the first sentence of the thread's constraint, repeated on every number, and it understated what a future team could build on. H. speculiger is also not one of the three species in the fin measurements this thread uses (Cheilopogon furcatus, Exocoetus volitans, Hirundichthys rondeleti), so using its sequence beside those measurements is cross-species within Exocoetidae and is labelled as such wherever it appears. This is the second public self-correction by this thread; the first withdrew a proposed gja5a link to the fin-length story (see genotype/nanopubs/DECISIONS.md)." ;
    delphi:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/genotype-correction-annotated-flying-fish-genome-exists> ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-genotype-thread-claude-fable-5-1> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/genotype-correction-annotated-flying-fish-genome-exists> a delphi:EvidenceItem ;
    rdfs:label "The flying-fish draft genome paper, read in full, against the claim this project had published" ;
    dct:description "Read from the flying_fish_genome block of genotype/map.vetted.json, which was built by reading the paper's own full text through the thread's logged fetcher." ;
    delphi:statisticalTest "Verification against the primary source: the paper's full text was fetched through the thread's logged fetcher and every figure above was read from it, including a count of the strings \"RNA-seq\" and \"transcriptome\". No statistical test." ;
    prov:used <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/dataset/xu-2021-hirundichthys-speculiger-draft-genome> ;
    dct:source <https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/34306036/> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom sub:map ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://delphi-mission-control.ashenoy000.workers.dev/t/genotype/data.json> .
  <https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/34306036/> a prov:Entity ;
    dct:title "Draft Genome of the Mirrorwing Flyingfish (Hirundichthys speculiger)" ;
    dct:bibliographicCitation "Xu 2021 Frontiers in Genetics 12:695700" ;
    dct:identifier "PMID 34306036" , "doi:10.3389/fgene.2021.695700" ;
    delphi:context "full text read" ;
    rdfs:comment "We predicted 23,611 protein-coding genes in the mirrorwing flyingfish genome" .
